# Lesson 6: Integration Activities — Applying AI to Improve Living and Working Standards

> ACTIVITY:
  **Context.** The Regional Delegation launches a "Smart Community" challenge: teams must propose and prototype an AI-based solution that improves living or working standards in their locality (health post triage, crop-disease advice, market-price prediction, school attendance and early-warning, waste sorting, water-point monitoring, local-language information chatbot).
  **Task (groups of 3–4, 2 periods + preparation).**
  1. **Define** (Lesson 1): the problem, the type of AI involved (capability/functionality/approach) and the application area; justify why AI adds value.
  2. **Technique and system** (Lesson 3): select the AI technique(s) and describe the intelligent system architecture (sensing, connectivity, data/AI, services, users, security) in a labelled diagram.
  3. **Prototype** (Lesson 4): build a Teachable Machine model (image/audio/pose) or, where no device is available, a paper-trained decision rule from a small dataset; report samples per class, accuracy, confusion matrix, one improvement iteration and one bias experiment.
  4. **Development plan** (Lesson 5): map the full solution onto the nine development stages, naming tools/languages (Python libraries) and deployment target, with a monitoring plan.
  5. **Ethics** (Lesson 2): identify four ethical issues, a risk–benefit grid and the responsible-AI principles and laws applied (UNESCO, Law 2024/017), including data consent and human oversight.
  6. **Present** (8 min): pitch with demo of the prototype; answer a panel's questions.
  **Criteria.** Relevance and clarity of problem and AI classification; sound technique/system design; working, evaluated prototype with evidence of iteration; realistic development plan and tools; depth of ethical analysis; presentation quality and teamwork.

## Rubric

| Criterion | 4 – Excellent | 3 – Good | 2 – Developing | 1 – Beginning |
| Problem & AI classification | Precise, well-justified, correct types | Mostly correct | Vague or partly incorrect | Missing |
| Technique & system design | Appropriate techniques, complete layered diagram with security | Minor gaps | Incomplete | Inappropriate |
| Prototype & evaluation | Works; accuracy/confusion matrix reported; iteration and bias experiment documented | Works; limited evaluation | Partially works | None |
| Development plan & tools | All stages, realistic tools, monitoring | Most stages | Few stages | Absent |
| Ethics & responsibility | Four issues, grid, principles, law, safeguards | Three issues, principles | Superficial | Missing |
| Presentation & teamwork | Clear demo, shared roles, confident answers | Clear | Uneven | Weak |

